    {
      "id": "dbtlu12",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Vaccination"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cn70p3m",
      "content": "• Vaccines stimulate the immune system to produce antibodies."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pebam9x",
      "content": "• They protect against diseases such as polio, measles and hepatitis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6a8r99s",
      "content": "• Vaccination is one of the most effective methods of disease prevention."
    },
    {
      "id": "zhe09vn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Prevention of Diseases"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "baozkrn",
      "content": "• Maintain personal hygiene."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5pb37hq",
      "content": "• Eat a balanced diet."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3u56t1v",
      "content": "• Drink clean water."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Distinguish between innate immunity (non-specific, present at birth) and acquired immunity (pathogen-specific, memory-based).",
        "Memorize vitamin and mineral deficiency diseases (e.g., Vitamin A - Night Blindness, Vitamin C - Scurvy, Vitamin D - Rickets, Iron - Anemia).",
        "Understand vectors and causative agents for common communicable diseases like Malaria (Protozoa), Tuberculosis (Bacteria), and Dengue (Virus)."
      ],
      "id": "xxzc9lm"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "swz10o0",
      "content": "• Regular vaccination."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7whq8jl",
      "content": "• Control insects and mosquitoes."
    },
    {
      "id": "gp3ryd1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dehgoc4",
      "content": "• Vaccines help build immunity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "muf2v15",
      "content": "• Vitamin deficiencies cause several diseases."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6f0814k",
      "content": "• Pathogens include bacteria, viruses, fungi and parasites."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5da1gcg",
      "content": "• The immune system defends the body against infections."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
